  "notes": [
    "An approved coding loop used to read **Stale** as soon as any later commit",
    "landed, because the check compared the approved tree with the current HEAD.",
    "That offered the Architect a wrong Reopen. The Git snapshot now also reports",
    "the first commit after the approved HEAD on the current first-parent history.",
    "An approval resolves Committed when that commit carries the approved tree, and",
    "it names that commit rather than the current HEAD.",
    "Git trouble is never read as approval or as stale history: only two exact",
    "\"not found\" / \"not an ancestor\" exits count as divergence evidence. A"
